how to migrate off of microsoft and other closed-source software

Operating system
if you know nothing about linux or bash: Linux mint is recommended, very stable, looks similar to windows, little to no terminal knowledge required. 
Less customisable, but very good for daily driving. Lindows is also an option (not linspire), but it is far less stable. 
For gaming, we recommend bazzite, with enhanced performance. a little higher maintainance, but worth it for a dedicated gaming machine. 
If you are tired of the appearance of windows, try ubuntu, or if you trust yourself to do a little maintainence, debian. 
Both with a very different appearance from windows, customisable dock especially with dash to dock extension, and easy access to custom keyboard shortcuts. 
If you are already experienced with computers and are willing to risk stability for the newest features, try fedora. Higher maintainance, but very efficient when used right.

Microsoft software
For the office suite, obviously LibreOffice, its practically the same, but free. for VSCode, use vscodium. No question there. For github, just use git in your terminal.


